# Ofir's portfolio website

One-page site with full case studies, deployed via GitHub Pages from this repo's `main` branch
(GitHub: `avitano/Avitano.Studio`). Live domain connected and working.

## Git discipline — read this first

**Never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git add`, `git merge`, or `git reset` without asking Ofir
first and getting an explicit go-ahead, every single time, no exceptions for "small" or "obvious"
changes.** Ofir always runs git operations himself. When a change is ready, stop and tell him
what changed and why, and let him review and commit it. Do not chain git write-commands into a
larger shell command to route around a denylist either — the rule is "ask first," not "avoid the
specific blocked command."

Reading state is fine any time: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`.

`main` is what GitHub Pages deploys. Anything not ready to go live belongs on another branch.

## Where things live

- Repo root = site root. `index.html` is the homepage: a single self-contained file (Tailwind v4
  browser build + inline `<style>`/`<script>`, no build step).
- Case studies: one folder per project at repo root, each `<Project-Name>/index.html`
  (Title-Case-With-Hyphens), e.g. `Digital-Loans/index.html`.
- `assets/` holds images/video. `assets/source - do not touch/` is a manual backup of raw exports,
  never write into it (it's gitignored).
- `BACKLOG.md` (gitignored, not on GitHub) is Ofir's running task list — check it for open work.
- `index-draft*.html` and `_to_delete/` are scratch/inert files, gitignored, not part of the live
  site. Don't treat them as source of truth for anything.

## No shared components — this matters a lot

**Every HTML file is fully independent.** No include/template system. Shared chrome (nav,
contact/footer, CSS variables, JS) is duplicated in full inside every single `index.html`. Any fix
to shared chrome must be hand-applied to every file: the homepage plus every case-study folder.
Trial a new shared-chrome pattern on one file first, confirm it live with Ofir, only then roll it
out to the rest.

## Tailwind v4 gotchas (silent failures, no console error)

1. This site's custom CSS is **unlayered** (written directly inside
   `<style type="text/tailwindcss">` after `@import "tailwindcss"`). An unlayered custom rule
   always beats a layered Tailwind utility, regardless of specificity or breakpoint. Never rely on
   a Tailwind utility class to override a property already set by a custom class on the same
   element — write real `@media` blocks in the custom CSS instead.
2. A CSS custom property (`--token`) that's only ever referenced inline (`style="..."` or JS)
   never gets emitted into `:root` by the browser-JIT compiler — it silently falls back to
   default/inherited with zero warning. Any `--token` you add or reuse needs at least one real
   occurrence inside the `<style type="text/tailwindcss">` block itself (a one-property CSS class
   is enough if the real usage is inline/JS-driven).

## Design system (DSM) — a starting point, not a mandate

The DSM (color/type tokens, pill buttons, no shadows, no dark card skins) is the site's current
default look, not a hard requirement. Ofir is actively reconsidering whether a strict DSM
constraint even fits a portfolio this size, and wants room to try genuinely new UI directions,
especially on exploratory/draft files (`index-draft*.html` and similar). Feel free to depart from
DSM tokens and patterns there if it serves the design better. It's fine to still reference or reuse
DSM tokens where they help, no need to avoid mentioning the DSM. When you do depart from it, say
plainly what you kept vs. changed and why, so Ofir can react to it live rather than discovering it
buried in a diff. For the *live* homepage and existing case-study pages (not drafts), stay closer
to the current look unless Ofir explicitly says otherwise for that specific piece of work.

Visual base: white page background, near-black/deep-teal primary (`#022c22`), emerald accent used
sparingly and never as a button color. Inter Tight for headings, Inter for body. Fully pill-shaped
buttons, 12-column grid, generous whitespace, `px-4 lg:px-20` horizontal padding on every section.

## Working style

- Step-by-step on anything visual/structural/new: state the plan, wait for an explicit go, make
  that one change, report, wait for the next instruction. Well-scoped bug fixes (a clear
  screenshot + description, including layout/CSS bugs) can just be fixed directly.
- No em-dashes, ever, in copy or code comments.
- English-only copy on the site.
- Before deleting or destructively overwriting any asset, flag it and ask, don't assume it's safe.
- Don't backfill an unfinished section with "more to come" placeholder copy — let it end cleanly.
- Full standing-rules reference (deeper detail than fits here) lives in the `avitano-portfolio-site-2026`
  Claude skill, which Ofir also uses in Claude/Cowork sessions on this same repo — ask him if
  something here seems incomplete rather than guessing.
